<title>UK: NWE OIL PRODUCTS MOSTLY WEAKER.</title>
<headline>NWE OIL PRODUCTS MOSTLY WEAKER.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE oil products were mostly weaker on Monday.</p>
<p>Gasoline lost up to $6.00 a tonne as U.S. buying interest waned and the spectre of fresh supplies from the end of this week and August 20 onwards impacted.</p>
<p>Gas oil shed $1.50 a tonne in line with August IPE which settled at $168.00. Volume was thin but spreads were firm. A heating oil barge moved at August IPE +$1 for second half August.</p>
</text>
